6,0 98.42591,8.10093,0 98.42522,8.10081,0 98.42417,8.09967,0 98.42411,8.09858,0 98.4252,8.09664,0 98.42488,8.09523,0 98.4177,8.08566,0 98.4146,8.08521,0 98.41506,8.07841,0 98.40125,8.05456,0</coordinates></LinearRing></outerBoundaryIs></Polygon></MultiGeometry></Placemark><Placemark><name>Thalang</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Heritage town, rainforest park and the local DJ scene</b><br>The inland north, the island's historic heart, near the airport. Wat Phra Thong, the Heroines Monument and the Thalang National Museum tell Phuket's history. To the east, Khao Phra Thaeo forest has Bang Pae waterfall, a gibbon project and an elephant sanctuary. Enthusiast Place, a DJ studio, is near Bang Tao.<br><br>Stay here if you want cheap, local and close to the airport, and you will drive to the beach and to parties.]]></description><styleUrl>#a-thalang</styleUrl><MultiGeometry><Polygon><outerBoundaryIs><LinearRing><coordinates>98.30435,8.04647,0 98.30932,8.04587,0 98.3122,8.04452,0 98.31315,8.0429,0 98.3101,8.02927,0 98.31303,8.02522,0 98.31304,8.02249,0 98.31372,8.02149,0 98.31633,8.02184,0 98.31831,8.01672,0 98.31884,8.01215,0 98.31986,8.01046,0 98.31972,8.00956,0 98.32119,8.00889,0 98.32159,8.00739,0 98.32381,8.00611,0 98.32423,8.00422,0 98.32388,8.00116,0 98.32321,7.99961,0 98.32072,7.99755,0 98.31997,7.99558,0 98.32059,7.99448,0 98.3168,7.99311,0 98.31628,7.99214,0 98.31622,7.99077,0 98.31285,7.9793,0 98.3126,7.97496,0 98.31303,7.97363,0 98.31179,7.96917,0 98.31158,7.96702,0 98.31033,7.96342,0 98.30875,7.96174,0 98.3118,7.9592,0 98.31392,7.95662,0 98.31509,7.9543,0 98.31564,7.95084,0 98.31617,7.94999,0 98.31823,7.94926,0 98.3278,7.94841,0 98.33654,7.94911,0 98.34173,7.94742,0 98.3426,7.94639,0 98.34354,7.94374,0 98.34413,7.94318,0 98.34739,7.94144,0 98.34806,7.94144,0 98.34958,7.94322,0 98.35378,7.94342,0 98.35425,7.94446,0 98.35412,7.94579,0 98.35533,7.94708,0 98.35618,7.94898,0 98.35238,7.95405,0 98.35239,7.95514,0 98.35373,7.95758,0 98.35542,7.95862,0 98.35569,7.95988,0 98.35828,7.96201,0 98.35943,7.96415,0 98.36866,7.96839,0 98.37148,7.96714,0 98.37226,7.96722,0 98.37322,7.96954,0 98.37534,7.97106,0 98.37552,7.97312,0 98.37652,7.97453,0 98.37765,7.97443,0 98.3786,7.9756,0 98.37974,7.97489,0 98.38311,7.97431,0 98.38521,7.97066,0 98.38656,7.97074,0 98.38767,7.96904,0 98.39103,7.96916,0 98.39324,7.96798,0 98.39435,7.96625,0 98.39555,7.96551,0 98.39552,7.96605,0 98.39659,7.96727,0 98.39771,7.96795,0 98.39461,7.97029,0 98.39551,7.97511,0 98.39417,7.97651,0 98.39432,7.97736,0 98.39306,7.97868,0 98.39516,7.98046,0 98.39594,7.98211,0 98.39354,7.98306,0 98.39206,7.9804,0 98.39099,7.98005,0 98.38962,7.98038,0 98.38927,7.98144,0 98.38974,7.98289,0 98.38943,7.98422,0 98.38848,7.98356,0 98.38762,7.98476,0 98.38602,7.98516,0 98.38579,7.98464,0 98.38645,7.98385,0 98.38624,7.98277,0 98.38583,7.9825,0 98.38573,7.98354,0 98.38474,7.98348,0 98.38448,7.98458,0 98.38304,7.98412,0 98.38297,7.98343,0 98.37981,7.98393,0 98.37903,7.98616,0 98.37868,7.98585,0 98.37733,7.98606,0 98.37629,7.98726,0 98.37513,7.98738,0 98.37334,7.98957,0 98.37256,7.98962,0 98.37008,7.99225,0 98.36969,7.99339,0 98.37177,7.99793,0 98.37129,7.99688,0 98.4103,8.01044,0 98.41065,8.01244,0 98.41042,8.01322,0 98.4117,8.01365,0 98.41022,8.0135,0 98.40985,8.01837,0 98.41107,8.02625,0 98.41264,8.0267,0 98.4152,8.03362,0 98.41499,8.03421,0 98.40713,8.03886,0 98.40125,8.05456,0 98.41506,8.07841,0 98.4146,8.08521,0 98.41204,8.08515,0 98.40977,8.08351,0 98.40924,8.08172,0 98.40717,8.07989,0 98.40642,8.07979,0 98.40616,8.07901,0 98.40601,8.07965,0 98.40316,8.08058,0 98.40139,8.08295,0 98.39984,8.08151,0 98.39836,8.08098,0 98.39747,8.07955,0 98.39656,8.07946,0 98.39526,8.08185,0 98.39264,8.08241,0 98.38857,8.08491,0 98.38666,8.08497,0 98.38606,8.08534,0 98.38612,8.08619,0 98.38276,8.09133,0 98.38255,8.09068,0 98.38268,8.09145,0 98.3809,8.0927,0 98.38139,8.09305,0 98.37981,8.09417,0 98.3762,8.09945,0 98.37338,8.1113,0 98.37432,8.11397,0 98.37459,8.11393,0 98.37546,8.11582,0 98.37413,8.11811,0 98.37043,8.12047,0 98.36744,8.12037,0 98.3632,8.11596,0 98.36261,8.11607,0 98.36233,8.11532,0 98.36108,8.11473,0 98.36023,8.11331,0 98.35923,8.11366,0 98.3584,8.11317,0 98.35684,8.11328,0 98.35505,8.11177,0 98.35513,8.11043,0 98.35312,8.11259,0 98.35221,8.11184,0 98.35207,8.11065,0 98.35155,8.11094,0 98.34874,8.10604,0 98.34882,8.10516,0 98.34753,8.1034,0 98.34835,8.10108,0 98.34784,8.09792,0 98.34653,8.09809,0 98.34365,8.09656,0 98.3422,8.09668,0 98.34125,8.09558,0 98.33574,8.09139,0 98.331,8.09056,0 98.31538,8.07597,0 98.31274,8.06088,0 98.31213,8.05889,0 98.31091,8.05817,0 98.31188,8.05506,0 98.31186,8.05353,0 98.31132,8.05233,0 98.30435,8.04647,0</coordinates></LinearRing></outerBoundaryIs></Polygon></MultiGeometry></Placemark><Placemark><name>Natai &amp; Khao Pilai (Phang Nga)</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Empty beach, Baba Beach Club and Circoloco Saturdays</b><br>About 10 km of wide, pale sand on the mainland north of the Sarasin Bridge, 35 minutes from the airport. No vendors, sunbeds or jet skis, and only a few resorts, most of them luxury. Baba Beach Club has a Funktion-One sound system and hosts Circoloco on Sat 9 and Sat 16 Jan, 15:00-03:00. You need a car or Grab.<br><br>Stay here if you find a room: on the Circoloco Saturdays (9, 16 and 23 Jan) rooms are sold out or very expensive, so this guide suggests Kamala and a driver.]]></description><styleUrl>#a-natai</styleUrl><MultiGeometry><Polygon><outerBoundaryIs><LinearRing><coordinates>98.26173,8.338,0 98.26453,8.3235,0 98.26491,8.31934,0 98.26662,8.31525,0 98.26917,8.30702,0 98.27324,8.28691,0 98.27791,8.26722,0 98.28172,8.24695,0 98.28224,8.23957,0 98.28187,8.23843,0 98.2799,8.23676,0 98.28041,8.23516,0 98.27993,8.23468,0 98.28046,8.23429,0 98.28063,8.23273,0 98.2811,8.232,0 98.302,8.232,0 98.302,8.338,0 98.26173,8.338,0</coordinates></LinearRing></outerBoundaryIs></Polygon></MultiGeometry></Placemark></Folder>
<Folder><name>Music &amp; raves</name><Placemark><name>Shelter Phuket (small club room inside Illuzion)</name><description><![CDATA[Shelter Phuket, 31 Bangla Road, Patong (behind the Illuzion main stage)<br>2027-01-08, 2027-01-09, 2027-01-15, 2027-01-16, 2027-01-22, 2027-01-23<br>Small club room behind the Illuzion main stage on Bangla Road, for about 500 people, with a Funktion-One sound system. Resident and guest DJs play house, tech house, minimal and some techno, mostly on Fridays and Saturdays. Not a Berlin-style club, but the most music-focused room in Patong.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-event</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.29747,7.89346,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Illuzion Phuket</name><description><![CDATA[Illuzion, 31 Bangla Road, Patong<br>Open every night 21:00-04:00 (Google Maps). Guest DJs mostly on Saturdays; in high season also on some Thursdays and Fridays (Jan 2026: Thu 8, Fri 9, Thu 15, Sat 17, Sat 24 Jan). In Oct 2026 the Friday main-room nights were NOTORIOUS (hip-hop). In 19-25 Jan: expect guests on Fri 22 or Sat 23 Jan. Also open on Mon 25 Jan.<br>Phuket's biggest club, for about 5,000 people, on Bangla Road. DJ Mag Top 100 Clubs 2026 lists it at number 9. The main room is big and commercial: EDM, house and tech house guests, and hip-hop on some Fridays (NOTORIOUS). Big LED wall and stage shows. For a smaller room, try Shelter in the same building.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-event</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.29744,7.89346,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>BOA Phuket (house club)</name><description><![CDATA[BOA Nightclub Phuket, 9/1 Bangla Road (Soi Gonzo), Patong<br>Open most nights from 21:00; guest DJ nights mostly on Fridays, Saturdays and some Sundays. In 19-25 Jan: likely Fri 22 and Sat 23 Jan.<br>House music club on Bangla Road, in Soi Gonzo, about 150 m west of Illuzion. It has several levels around one big dance floor and an Adamson sound system. Resident and guest DJs play house, tech house and afro house. Some nights are free. More stylish than underground, but a good house option in Patong.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-event</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.29617,7.89373,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Café del Mar Phuket</name><description><![CDATA[Café del Mar Phuket Beach Club, north end of Kamala Beach<br>Open daily; Club Room Wed-Sat from 22:00; Pyramid Stage shows on set dates. In 19-25 Jan: Club Room Wed 20 to Sat 23 Jan. Pyramid shows not announced yet.<br>Ibiza beach club at the north end of Kamala Beach, close to your base. Big DJs play afternoon-to-night shows on the outdoor Pyramid Stage: Argy on Fri 8 Jan and Marco Carola on Wed 13 Jan. Nothing is announced yet for 18-25 Jan. The Club Room has DJ nights Wed-Sat from 22:00. Stylish and expensive, not underground.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-event</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.28394,7.96102,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Courage Bar (FAKE PALM, SUB and Enthusiast nights)</name><description><![CDATA[COURAGE | КУРАЖ, 16 Bangkok Road, Phuket Old Town<br>Irregular parties in high season, mostly on Fridays or Saturdays. Last January: Framework with Sergey Sanchez (Fri 2 Jan 2026), FAKE ORBIT (Sat 17 Jan 2026) and a SUB boat party from Chalong Pier (Tue 27 Jan 2026).<br>Small bar in Phuket Old Town. In the 2025/26 season it hosted some of Phuket's most underground parties: FAKE PALM (techno, breaks), SUB (UK garage, bass, jungle) and WAV.e x Enthusiast (minimal). Parties are not weekly. No dates for 19-25 Jan yet (16 Oct 2026).]]></description><styleUrl>#p-event</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.38185,7.87917,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Open Doors Tuesday at Enthusiast Place</name><description><![CDATA[Enthusiast Place, Srisoonthorn Road, Si Sunthon, Thalang<br>2027-01-12, 2027-01-19<br>DJ studio and music space of the Enthusiast crew (minimal, deep tech house), with CDJ-3000s, Technics turntables and modular synths. Every Tuesday from 19:00 it opens its doors for free: you can play, jam and meet people. It is a meeting place, not a club. Go to meet Phuket's underground DJs.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-event</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.32658,7.97912,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>OXA Jungle Party</name><description><![CDATA[OXA - Jungle Party, 72/52 Moo 2, Ban Tai, Koh Phangan<br>2027-01-08, 2027-01-15, 2027-01-19<br>Big weekly jungle party in Ban Tai with three floors: Oasis (tech house, indie dance), Canyon (techno) and Cabin (hip-hop, commercial). Fire shows open the night. Busy and touristy, with VIP areas. In Full Moon week it moves from Friday to Tue 19 Jan. Tickets for 8, 15 and 19 Jan are on sale.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-event</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>100.03195,9.71735,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Sabaii Friday Beach Party (Ban Tai)</name><description><![CDATA[Sabaii Bay Beach Club, Ban Tai Beach, Koh Phangan<br>2027-01-08, 2027-01-15, 2027-01-22<br>Free weekly beach party at Sabaii Bay Beach Club on Ban Tai Beach. A sunset session starts at 17:00 and the main party at 20:00. Local DJs play a mix of house and techno. Relaxed and social, not a hard rave. On Fri 22 Jan it is a sunset warm-up before the Full Moon Party in Haad Rin.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-event</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>100.00255,9.70682,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Retro Mountain Jungle Club</name><description><![CDATA[Retro Mountain Jungle Club, Ban Tai, Koh Phangan<br>Usually 1-3 party nights a week; the program changes every week<br>Jungle club on a hill in Ban Tai, Koh Phangan, with two stages and a rain-proof main dance floor. Different crews run the nights: hard techno 'Secret Rave' by Hardtechno KPG, Kovër Crëw techno nights, psytrance, and guests like Nakadia. One of the best places on the islands for dark, hard techno.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-event</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>100.03807,9.72188,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Lighthouse Party (Haad Rin)</name><description><![CDATA[Lighthouse Bungalows, Haad Rin, Koh Phangan<br>2027-01-08, 2027-01-12, 2027-01-15, 2027-01-19<br>Techno party on the rocks at the end of Leela Beach, Haad Rin. You walk along the beach and over a bridge above the sea. Local and international DJs play deep house, techno and progressive until sunrise. Tuesdays all year, Fridays too in high season. Smaller and more underground than the Full Moon Party.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-event</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>100.07051,9.66689,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Chill Up: Monday Madness and Phangan Calling</name><description><![CDATA[Chill UP club, 114/2 Moo 1, Ban Tai main road, Koh Phangan<br>2027-01-11, 2027-01-14, 2027-01-18, 2027-01-21<br>Free-entry bar and mini club on Ban Tai main road, open since 2015. Monday Madness plays progressive house, minimal and techno. Thursday Phangan Calling plays indie dance, tech house and techno. Music until 02:00, closed Wednesdays. Other nights are psytrance (Tue, Fri) and drum and bass (Sat).]]></description><styleUrl>#p-event</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>100.01003,9.70559,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Eden Garden Saturday (Haad Yuan)</name><description><![CDATA[Eden Garden, Haad Yuan Beach, Koh Phangan<br>2027-01-09, 2027-01-16, 2027-01-23<br>Long-running free Saturday party on the rocks at Haad Yuan, a small beach north of Haad Rin. Mostly house and tech house, with some progressive and techno, from 21:00 until late Sunday morning. Sat 23 Jan is the night after the Full Moon Party. Go by taxi boat from Haad Rin or by 4x4 truck from Ban Tai.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-event</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>100.07599,9.6933,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Unclave (Groovy Tunes minimal nights)</name><description><![CDATA[Unclave, Ban Tai hills, Koh Phangan<br>2027-01-08, 2027-01-22<br>Underground club in the jungle hills above Ban Tai (RA: room for 500). Home of Groovy Tunes, a minimal and deep house party about every second Friday, 22:00 to sunrise. If the rhythm holds, the next dates are Fri 8 and Fri 22 Jan. Fri 22 is Full Moon night, so it may move.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-event</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>100.04231,9.73006,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Waterfall Festival</name><description><![CDATA[Waterfall Festival site, Ban Tai, Koh Phangan<br>2027-01-13, 2027-01-20, 2027-01-24<br>Big jungle party next to a waterfall in Ban Tai, with five stages: house and melodic techno with lasers on the main stage, plus psytrance, hip-hop and afrobeat. It runs 2 nights before and 2 nights after each Full Moon Party, so expect Wed 20 and Sun 24 Jan. Very touristy.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-event</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>100.04692,9.70588,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Deep Sundays at Pangea Beach Bar (Koh Lanta)</name><description><![CDATA[Pangea Beach Bar & Kitchen, Long Beach (Phra Ae), Koh Lanta<br>2027-01-10, 2027-01-17, 2027-01-24<br>Beach bar on Long Beach, Koh Lanta, known for deep and minimal house since 2012. It booked Ian Pooley, Clive Henry and Nakadia in past years. In high season it runs 'Deep Sundays' from 18:00 with sunset DJ sets, last seen in March 2026. Small (about 300 people). Only worth it if you stay on Koh Lanta.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-event</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>99.03373,7.60588,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Circoloco Thailand 2027</name><description><![CDATA[Baba Beach Club Natai (Baba Beach Jungle)<br>2027-01-09, 2027-01-16, 2027-01-23<br>The famous Monday party from DC-10 Ibiza, on Natai Beach north of Phuket. Three Saturdays (9, 16 and 23 Jan), 3 PM to 3 AM, from sunny afternoon to night by the sea. House, tech house and some techno. Sat 23 Jan is the last one. The 2027 lineup is not out yet. In 2026: Michael Bibi, Palms Trax, Adriatique.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-event</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.2817659,8.2502954,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Argy at Café del Mar (Pyramid Stage)</name><description><![CDATA[Café del Mar Phuket, Pyramid Stage<br>2027-01-08<br>Argy plays the Pyramid Stage at Café del Mar on your arrival day: melodic house and techno on the beach at Kamala, from the afternoon to 22:30, then an after-party in the Clubroom.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-event</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.2839357,7.9610227,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Marco Carola at Café del Mar</name><description><![CDATA[Café del Mar Phuket, Pyramid Stage<br>2027-01-13<br>Marco Carola, the man behind the Music On residency in Ibiza, plays one of his long sets on the open-air Pyramid Stage. Nicolas Masseyeff supports. Big beach-club crowd, tech house and techno from afternoon into the night. The biggest techno-side name in Phuket in your dates so far.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-event</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.2839357,7.9610227,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Halfmoon Festival</name><description><![CDATA[Halfmoon Magic Forest, Ban Tai (Day 2). Day 1 at Harmony Beach Club<br>2027-01-03, 2027-01-04, 2027-01-15, 2027-01-16, 2027-01-31<br>Koh Phangan's big two-day jungle festival, now in its 23rd year. Day 1 is a beach party at Harmony Beach Club. Day 2 is the main night in the Magic Forest with 3 stages: psytrance, melodic techno and tech house, and hip-hop. Your edition is Fri 15 and Sat 16 Jan.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-event</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>100.0302665,9.7133568,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Daft Funk Live (Daft Punk tribute)</name><description><![CDATA[Banana Beach Club by Sollis 2.0<br>2027-01-14<br>A full live band plays Daft Punk songs note for note, with the helmets and a big light rig. At the new beach club on small Banana Beach, between Layan and Nai Thon (not the Banana Beach on Coral Island). A fun party night, not underground. Part of a three-city Thailand tour by Midnight Sun.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-event</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.2770875,8.0424305,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>O Beach Ibiza x Barra Cuda</name><description><![CDATA[Barra Cuda Beach Club, Patong<br>2027-01-01, 2027-01-06, 2027-01-08, 2027-01-13, 2027-01-15, 2027-01-20, 2027-01-27<br>The Ibiza pool-party brand O Beach returns to Barra Cuda Beach Club on Patong Beach. Two pools and a pool dance floor, with dancers, shows and commercial house from noon to midnight. Very touristy, but a big party if you stay in Patong. This is the 'Barra Cuda Phuket' seen on listing sites.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-event</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.296207,7.8976887,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>MACAN live in Phuket</name><description><![CDATA[Lotus Arena Phuket, Cherng Talay<br>2027-01-08<br>Big solo concert by MACAN, one of the most popular Russian-language artists today. He plays his hits with a full live show at Lotus Arena, a large open-air concert venue in Cherng Talay. Not electronic music, but a big night for Russian-speaking fans. It is on your arrival day.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-event</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.310065,7.984822,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Carl Cox at Café del Mar</name><description><![CDATA[Café del Mar Phuket, Pyramid Stage<br>2027-01-03<br>Techno and house legend Carl Cox returns to the open-air Pyramid Stage at Café del Mar, with Nic Fanciulli playing before him. Beach-club show from afternoon to night, then an after-party inside. It is five days before you arrive, so only if you change your flights.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-event</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.2839357,7.9610227,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Francis Mercier at Café del Mar</name><description><![CDATA[Café del Mar Phuket, Pyramid Stage<br>2027-01-06<br>Afro house star Francis Mercier comes back to Café del Mar after his debut album Lakay (Home). This time he plays the big open-air Pyramid Stage. Beach-club party from afternoon to night. It is two days before you arrive.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-event</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.2839357,7.9610227,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>BLOND:ISH at Café del Mar</name><description><![CDATA[Café del Mar Phuket, Pyramid Stage<br>2027-01-07<br>BLOND:ISH, known for her Abracadabra residency at Pacha Ibiza, plays Phuket for the first time, on the Pyramid Stage at Café del Mar. Feel-good house for a big beach-club crowd. It is one day before you arrive.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-event</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.2839357,7.9610227,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>DnB Allstars Thailand 2027</name><description><![CDATA[Azulea, Chalong<br>2027-01-22, 2027-01-23, 2027-01-24<br>Three days of drum and bass at Azulea, an open-air site in the forest in Chalong, south Phuket. Pendulum (DJ set) is the first name, with 50+ international artists promised. Two stages, Void sound system, about 3,000 ravers and afterparties. The 2026 edition had Camo & Krooked, Turno, BOU and Grooverider.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-event</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3670781,7.8400875,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Zamna Phuket 2027</name><description><![CDATA[Yeden Gardens, Khok Kloi (Natai area)<br>2027-01-29, 2027-01-30<br>The Tulum festival brand Zamna comes to Phuket for the first time: two days at Yeden Gardens near Natai Beach. Zamna is known for big stage design and sound, and for melodic techno and house. No lineup yet. The ticket site says Fri 29 and Sat 30 Jan, after you fly home on 26 Jan.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-event</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.281809,8.26232,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Full Moon Party</name><description><![CDATA[Haad Rin Nok (Sunrise Beach), Haad Rin<br>2027-01-22<br>The famous all-night beach party on Haad Rin Nok (Sunrise Beach). About 20,000 people, neon paint, fire shows and a long row of bars, each with its own sound system: mostly EDM, plus house, techno, trance and hip-hop. Fun to see once, but the opposite of underground. It falls in your Koh Phangan days.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-event</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>100.0680833,9.6767778,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Jungle Experience</name><description><![CDATA[Jungle Experience, Ban Tai<br>2027-01-21<br>Koh Phangan's classic jungle rave, running since 2009. Two stages: house and techno on the Dragon stage, drum and bass on the other. Fire shows, neon paint and a pro Muay Thai ring. Each monthly edition is the night before the Full Moon Party, so expect Thu 21 Jan. This date is not on sale yet.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-event</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>100.0299359,9.715354,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Sunset Connections at LEVITATE Viewpoint</name><description><![CDATA[LEVITATE Viewpoint, Kamala-Patong hill road (Phra Barami Road), Patong<br>2027-01-08, 2027-01-15, 2027-01-22<br>Sunset lounge on the hill road between Kamala and Patong, about 7 minutes by car from your base. Every Friday from 16:00 it runs Sunset Connections: free entry, sea views, live DJs and deep grooves until about midnight. A warm-up or a chill night, not a rave.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-event</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.2802167,7.9206553,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Armania Phuket (house club)</name><description><![CDATA[Armania Phuket, 11 Bangla Road, Patong<br>Open every night 22:00-04:00; guest DJ nights mostly on Fridays (in your dates: Fri 8, 15 and 22 Jan).<br>Upscale VIP club on Bangla Road, Patong, with a Renaissance-style interior. Guest DJs play mostly on Fridays: house and tech house, often well-known names. In January 2026 it had Toolroom, Meduza and Wax Motif. Polished and commercial, not underground. One more option for a Friday in Patong.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-event</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.2963714,7.8939004,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>EXPEREMINT and Zonda nights at Summerset Bar &amp; Lounge</name><description><![CDATA[Summerset Bar & Lounge, 177/29 Moo 4, Srisoonthorn Road, Si Sunthon (Bang Tao side)<br>Irregular so far: EXPEREMINT on Fri 11 Sep and Zonda on Fri 16 Oct 2026. January dates not announced.<br>Small lounge bar near Laguna and Bang Tao, 300 m from Enthusiast Place. Since Sep 2026 it hosts underground nights: EXPEREMINT by the Enthusiast crew (deep, tech, minimal) and Zonda (underground tech house). The crew wants a room where the music is the reason people come. No January dates yet.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-event</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3293446,7.9795397,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Sound Club Samui</name><description><![CDATA[Sound Club Samui, Soi Green Mango, Chaweng<br>Open every night (Google Maps: 22:00-06:00). Guest nights on some dates; January 2027 guests not announced.<br>Long-running late club in Soi Green Mango, Chaweng, open until about 6 AM. Resident DJs play house and tech house most nights. Some nights have techno guests: Nakadia (Jan 2025 and Sat 3 Oct 2026) and Stella Bossi (Jan 2025 and 3 Jan 2026). A good late option if you are on Samui.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-event</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>100.0628818,9.5325738,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Seaside Beach Party (Haad Rin West)</name><description><![CDATA[SEASIDE SUNSET bar, Haad Rin Nai (west side of Haad Rin), Koh Phangan<br>2027-01-14, 2027-01-18<br>Sunset-to-sunrise beach party at Seaside Sunset Bar on the quiet west side of Haad Rin, run by the Solar Conexion crew. Melodic house, techno and deep grooves, a fire show and an art market. In Jan 2026 it ran every Thursday. In Full Moon weeks it often moves to a Monday 'pre-Full Moon' party.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-event</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>100.0597003,9.6797573,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>WET! Full Moon Week Pool Parties (Haad Rin)</name><description><![CDATA[Wet! a Pool Party Hostel by Wild & Wandering, 132 Haad Rin, Koh Phangan<br>2027-01-20, 2027-01-21, 2027-01-22, 2027-01-23, 2027-01-24<br>Free hostel pool parties in Haad Rin on each afternoon of Full Moon week, from 15:00 into the night. Regular DJs play house, tech house and techno. The usual order: Waterfall pre-party, Jungle Experience pre-party, Full Moon pool party, then a recovery, foam or karaoke party. Young backpacker crowd.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-event</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>100.0648796,9.6765162,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bambu Sunday Session (Haad Yuan)</name><description><![CDATA[Bambu Huts, Haad Yuan, Koh Phangan<br>2027-01-10, 2027-01-17, 2027-01-24<br>Sunday day party at Bambu Huts on Haad Yuan, the small beach next to Eden Garden. Two stages, a terrace and a garden, with DJs from house and afro to progressive and tech, fire shows and a small market. It starts in the afternoon and goes on into the night. A good Sunday after the Full Moon weekend.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-event</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>100.0754089,9.6934099,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Hollystone Saturday</name><description><![CDATA[Hollystone, 12/1 Moo 5, Koh Phangan (by a lake, north of Thong Sala)<br>2027-01-09, 2027-01-16, 2027-01-23<br>Open-air club by a lake in the hills north of Thong Sala, every Saturday since 2017. The dance floor is phone-free: no filming, just dancing. Its own label, Hollystone Records, sets the sound: indie dance and progressive house, with resident Vakabular and guests. Smaller and more focused than the big parties.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-event</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>99.9879296,9.7501471,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Utopia (jungle rave, Than Sadet)</name><description><![CDATA[Utopia site, Than Sadet-Ko Pha-Ngan National Park area, on the road to Thong Nai Pan<br>2027-01-20<br>Open-air jungle rave in the Than Sadet national park area, on the road to Thong Nai Pan. Born from psytrance, now also techno and house, with big names (Astrix 22 Dec, Infected Mushroom 31 Dec 2026). Since July 2026 most dates were two nights before the full moon, which would be Wed 20 Jan. Not announced yet.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-event</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>100.0517324,9.7409336,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder>
<Folder><name>Places to go</name><Placemark><name>Big Buddha</name><description><![CDATA[Must-see · 1–2 h<br>A 45 m white marble Buddha on top of Nakkerd Hill. It closed after a landslide in August 2024 and reopened on 3 March 2026. The terrace has wide views over Kata, Karon and Chalong Bay. It is an active temple, so dress and behave with respect.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3128,7.8276,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Wat Chalong</name><description><![CDATA[Must-see · 1–2 h<br>Phuket's largest and most important Buddhist temple. Climb the 60 m Grand Pagoda: the lower floors have Buddha statues and murals, and the top floor holds a small bone relic of the Buddha. Loud firecrackers are normal: locals light them to give thanks when a wish comes true.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3365,7.8468,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Phuket Old Town</name><description><![CDATA[Must-see · Half day<br>The historic center of Phuket Town. Colorful Sino-Portuguese shophouses from the tin-mining era line Thalang, Dibuk, Krabi and Phang Nga roads. Soi Romanee is the prettiest small lane. Come for cafes, street art, Chinese shrines and local food such as Hokkien noodles.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3892,7.8853,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Sunday Walking Street Market (Lard Yai)</name><description><![CDATA[Must-see · Evening<br>Every Sunday evening, Thalang Road in the Old Town closes to cars and becomes a 360 m street market. Stalls sell Phuket snacks, handmade crafts and clothes, with music and street shows. It is busy and local, and the old shophouses make a great backdrop.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3891,7.8848,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Promthep Cape</name><description><![CDATA[Must-see · 1–2 h<br>The southern tip of Phuket and the island's most famous sunset point. Terraces look west over the sea and small islands. Next to the white lighthouse (with a small free museum) is a Brahma shrine surrounded by hundreds of elephant statues. Expect big crowds at sunset.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3054,7.7619,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Windmill Viewpoint</name><description><![CDATA[Must-see · 1–2 h<br>A grassy hilltop next to a large wind turbine, between Nai Harn and Promthep Cape. You look down on small Ya Nui Beach and Koh Man island, with Promthep in the distance. There is a little parking, a shade pavilion and a drinks stall. A calm sunset choice.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3066,7.7697,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Black Rock Viewpoint (Pa Hin Dam)</name><description><![CDATA[Hidden gem · 1–2 h<br>One of the best views in south Phuket. From a rocky hilltop about 290 m high you see Nai Harn Bay, Ao Sane, Koh Man and Promthep Cape. Getting there takes effort: a bumpy dirt road, then a short, steep forest path. Few people, no shops, no railings.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-gem</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.2975,7.783,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Karon Viewpoint</name><description><![CDATA[Must-see · 1–2 h<br>Phuket's classic postcard view: three bays in a row. Kata Noi is below, then Kata with little Koh Pu island, and Karon further north. A quick 15-minute stop with a large car park and small drink stalls, on the way to Nai Harn and Promthep Cape.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3022,7.7973,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Kata Beach</name><description><![CDATA[Must-see · Half day<br>A 1.5 km bay of soft sand with Koh Pu island in front. From December to April the sea is usually calm and clear, good for swimming. It is more relaxed than Patong, with shade trees, beach restaurants and massages. The south end is the liveliest in the evening.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.2978,7.8203,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Kata Noi Beach</name><description><![CDATA[Must-see · Half day<br>A small, quieter bay just south of Kata, with soft white sand and clear water. In the dry season the sea is calm and good for swimming, and lifeguards work in the daytime. Most of the beachfront is taken by one big resort, Katathani, so there are few shops or bars.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.2988,7.8063,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Nai Harn Beach</name><description><![CDATA[Must-see · Half day<br>A wide, natural bay in the far south of the island. The land behind the sand is protected, so there are no buildings, only tall casuarina trees. The water is clear blue in high season. Simple Thai restaurants are across the small road, and a temple and lake are behind the beach.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3057,7.776,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Freedom Beach</name><description><![CDATA[Must-see · Half day<br>A 300 m cove of soft white sand and clear water just south of Patong. You arrive by longtail boat or by a steep jungle trail, so it is much calmer than the big beaches. There is some snorkeling at both ends. Barefoot Bistro at the south end serves food and drinks.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.2755,7.8749,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Patong Beach</name><description><![CDATA[Must-see · Half day<br>Phuket's busiest and most famous beach: 3 km of sand in front of the main party town. Expect jet skis, parasailing, vendors and crowds in the center. The north end is quieter, with softer sand and cleaner water. The south end has longtail boats to Freedom Beach.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.2957,7.8966,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bangla Road</name><description><![CDATA[Must-see · Evening<br>Patong's famous 400 m party street. Neon beer bars, go-go bars, live music bars and big clubs like Illuzion fill it every night. Loud, chaotic and worth seeing once. The music is mostly commercial EDM, hip-hop and cover bands, not underground techno.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.2968,7.8936,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Khao Rang Viewpoint</name><description><![CDATA[Must-see · 1–2 h<br>A green hill right above Phuket Town. A viewing deck looks over the city, Chalong Bay and Cape Panwa. Hilltop restaurants such as Tunk Ka Cafe serve Thai food with the same view. A good end to an Old Town day, especially at sunset.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3802,7.8924,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Rawai Seafood Market</name><description><![CDATA[Must-see · 1–2 h<br>A 100 m strip next to Rawai Pier, in an old sea gypsy fishing village. Fish stalls are on one side, restaurants on the other. You choose fish, prawns, crab or lobster, pay by weight, and a restaurant across the road cooks it your way. Fun, but no longer cheap.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3288,7.7756,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Naka Weekend Market</name><description><![CDATA[Must-see · Evening<br>Phuket's biggest weekend night market, on the south edge of Phuket Town. Hundreds of stalls sell cheap clothes, souvenirs and gadgets, plus a large street-food area. There is live music on the stage in the evening. Busy, hot and very local.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3663,7.8808,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Chillva Market</name><description><![CDATA[Must-see · Evening<br>A trendy night market in Phuket Town, popular with young Thais. Local fashion stalls and street food sit between bars built from stacked shipping containers, some with upstairs seats. A stage has live music. Smaller and more creative than Naka.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3734,7.9071,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Nai Yang Beach (Sirinat National Park)</name><description><![CDATA[Must-see · Half day<br>A quiet, shady bay inside Sirinat National Park, next to the airport. Small seafood restaurants and bars sit under the trees, and the sea is calm in high season. About 2.5 km north, at Mai Khao Beach, planes land low over the sand in the dry season.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.2976,8.09,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bang Pae Waterfall (Khao Phra Thaeo)</name><description><![CDATA[Must-see · 2–3 h<br>The largest waterfall on Phuket, inside the Khao Phra Thaeo rainforest reserve. A 10-15 minute jungle path follows the stream to the falls and rock pools. In January the flow is getting low, so think forest walk, not big waterfall. The Gibbon Rehabilitation Project is at the entrance.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3932,8.0415,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Phuket Elephant Sanctuary</name><description><![CDATA[Must-see · Half day<br>An ethical sanctuary for rescued and retired elephants. There is no riding, no bathing and, since 1 April 2026, no feeding. You watch the elephants roam, forage and bathe freely from forest trails and a long canopy walkway. Lunch is a vegetarian Thai buffet.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.4016,8.0258,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Chalong Bay Rum Distillery (The Distillery Phuket)</name><description><![CDATA[Must-see · 1–2 h<br>The Distillery Phuket, home of Chalong Bay Rum, was started in 2012 by two French expats. They make rum from fresh Thai sugarcane juice, plus Saneha gin and Lanna vodka. The 1-hour tour ends with a tasting and a mojito. The bar and restaurant in the sugarcane garden are good for dinner.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3523,7.8417,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Banana Beach</name><description><![CDATA[Hidden gem · Half day<br>Small cove with soft sand, clear water and rocks for snorkelling at both ends. Late in 2025 the old jungle path closed. Now you park at a new car park at the north end, next to a new beach club with music. The old family restaurant further south is still open.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-gem</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.2764,8.0419,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Laem Singh Beach</name><description><![CDATA[Hidden gem · Half day<br>A 300 m cove with golden sand, big granite boulders and clear water, between Surin and Kamala. The road access closed in 2017, so you come by a short boat ride or a rocky walk. Because of this it feels almost empty, even in high season. One small Thai restaurant on the rocks. No sunbeds, shops or toilets.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-gem</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.2795,7.9685,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ya Nui Beach</name><description><![CDATA[Hidden gem · 2–3 h<br>Tiny cove split in two by a small rocky hill, with the island Koh Man in front. Clear water and rocks make it one of the easiest snorkel spots in the south. You can rent kayaks and paddle boards. Two simple Thai restaurants under the trees. It is small, so it can be busy at peak times.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-gem</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3063,7.7675,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Tri Trang Beach</name><description><![CDATA[Hidden gem · 2–3 h<br>Quiet bay only a few kilometres south of Patong, but it feels far away. Palm trees, one row of beach chairs and the Rosewood resort behind. At low tide rocks and coral show, so swim at high tide. Good snorkelling near the rocks. Small cafes with big views sit on the hill road to Paradise Beach.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-gem</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.275,7.8863,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ao Yon Beach</name><description><![CDATA[Hidden gem · Half day<br>Long, quiet bay on the east side of the island, near Cape Panwa. Tall palm trees, a few small beach restaurants and bars, and mostly locals and long-time residents. It still feels like old Phuket. Good for a slow walk, lunch and a swim far from the west-coast crowds.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-gem</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3905,7.8118,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Layan Beach</name><description><![CDATA[Hidden gem · 2–3 h<br>Quiet north end of Bang Tao Bay. The sand runs north to a small river mouth, with a big island offshore. Locals and expats come for a long lunch, a swim and a massage. The small beach restaurants were removed. Tan Restaurant and Massage, where the road meets the beach, is the last one left.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-gem</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.289,8.0283,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Sai Kaew Beach</name><description><![CDATA[Hidden gem · 2–3 h<br>Long, empty white-sand beach at the far north tip of Phuket, just before the Sarasin Bridge. Shallow water, small waves in the dry season and kilometres of sand to walk. Only one bamboo restaurant is left on the sand, serving Thai seafood. Leatherback turtles sometimes nest on this coast from November to February.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-gem</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.2876,8.1895,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Laem Krating Viewpoint</name><description><![CDATA[Hidden gem · 2–3 h<br>Wild grassy cape on the south-west coast, west of Nai Harn Beach. After a rough 30-minute walk you get open sea views, big waves on the rocks and Promthep Cape in the distance. It stays quiet. There are no fences, signs or facilities, so it is only for fit walkers in dry weather.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-gem</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.2892,7.7763,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Khao Khad Viewpoint Tower</name><description><![CDATA[Hidden gem · 1–2 h<br>Small viewing tower on Khao Khad hill, on the road to Cape Panwa. From the top you get a 360-degree view: Chalong Bay, Phuket Town, Cape Panwa and many small islands. It is calmer than the big west-coast viewpoints. Free, with a car park, toilets and a few stalls at the bottom.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-gem</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3836,7.8347,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bang Rong Pier and Mangrove Walk</name><description><![CDATA[Hidden gem · 2–3 h<br>Small Muslim fishing village on the quiet north-east coast, with the pier for boats to Koh Yao. A wooden boardwalk goes through the mangroves to a floating community restaurant with fresh seafood and views of the boats. Kayaks can be rented to paddle into the mangrove channels; ask ahead.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-gem</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.4159,8.05,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Gibbon Rehabilitation Project</name><description><![CDATA[Hidden gem · 2–3 h<br>Small charity that rescues gibbons from the tourist trade and returns them to the forest. In a one-hour session a guide explains the work at the edge of Phuket's last rainforest. Only 36 visitors a day are allowed, to keep contact with the gibbons low. A calm, honest nature stop.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-gem</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3938,8.0419,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Koh Sirey: Hilltop Temple and Sea Gypsy Village</name><description><![CDATA[Hidden gem · 2–3 h<br>Small island joined to Phuket Town by a short bridge. On the hilltop, Wat Ban Koh Sirey has a long golden reclining Buddha and a wide view over Phuket Town. Below is Laem Tukkae, a working village of the Urak Lawoi sea people. It is quiet compared with the beach areas. Monkeys live near the bridge.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-gem</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.4263,7.8802,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Wat Phra Thong (Half-Buried Buddha)</name><description><![CDATA[Hidden gem · 1–2 h<br>Old temple in Thalang with a golden Buddha that comes out of the ground only from the chest up. Local legend says people tried to dig it out but could not. A small museum shows objects from Phuket's tin-mining past. Mostly local people come to pray, so it is calm and real.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-gem</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3377,8.034,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Phuket Mining Museum</name><description><![CDATA[Hidden gem · 1–2 h<br>Large air-conditioned museum about the tin mines that made Phuket rich long before tourism. It has a mine tunnel section, a big model mine with many small figures and a rebuilt old Phuket street with Chinese merchant life. Some parts look old and worn. Few foreign visitors come.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-gem</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3495,7.9333,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Soi Dog Foundation Sanctuary</name><description><![CDATA[Hidden gem · 1–2 h<br>Large shelter for street dogs and cats, run by a well-known charity. A free 45-minute guided tour explains their work and introduces some of the 1,800 animals in their care. After the tour you can spend time in the puppy area and the cat house. Tours are in English and Thai.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-gem</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3132,8.128,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Karon Temple Market</name><description><![CDATA[Hidden gem · Evening<br>Twice-a-week night market around Karon's old temple. Many street food stalls: pad thai, grilled skewers, chicken rice, mango sticky rice and fruit shakes. Also cheap clothes, carved soaps and souvenirs. Busy and fun, with a beautiful temple behind the stalls.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-gem</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.298,7.8479,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Kruvit Raft (Floating Seafood Restaurant)</name><description><![CDATA[Hidden gem · 2–3 h<br>Big wooden raft restaurant on the sea between Phuket and Koh Maphrao, listed in the 2026 Michelin Guide. Fish, crabs, prawns and oysters live in nets under the deck. You point at what you want and they cook it. Most guests are Thai. A fun and very local seafood meal.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-gem</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.4136,7.9348,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Summore Day Cafe</name><description><![CDATA[Hidden gem · 1–2 h<br>Hillside cafe, restaurant and bar with terraced gardens, a koi pond and a rooftop deck over Ya Nui Beach and Koh Man island. Serious coffee from their own roast, food from breakfast to steak, and cocktails with local Chalong Bay rum. Live music on weekend afternoons.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-gem</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3062,7.7642,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>View Cafe at Phuket (Phuket View Coffee and Resort)</name><description><![CDATA[Hidden gem · 1–2 h<br>Quiet hilltop cafe high above Bang Wad Reservoir. From terraces and small balconies you look over Phuket Town, the east coast, Chalong Bay and the islands. Simple Thai food, coffee and cold drinks. No tour buses; most guests are locals. Best on a clear day.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-gem</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3299,7.8701,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Phang Nga Bay: James Bond Island and sea caves</name><description><![CDATA[Day trip · Full day<br>A calm bay full of tall limestone islands. Tours stop at James Bond Island (Khao Phing Kan and the Ko Tapu rock), take you by canoe into sea caves and hidden lagoons at Panak or Hong island, and stop for lunch at Koh Panyee, a Muslim fishing village on stilts.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.50056,8.27538,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Hong by Starlight: evening sea-canoe trip</name><description><![CDATA[Day trip · Full day<br>John Gray's Sea Canoe runs this trip from midday into the night. You pass James Bond Island (from the boat), then guides paddle you into sea caves and hidden lagoons at Panak and Hong islands. You make a krathong (small floating offering), eat a Thai buffet at sunset, then paddle in the dark to see glowing plankton.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.50056,8.22444,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Phi Phi Islands and Maya Bay</name><description><![CDATA[Day trip · Full day<br>The famous islands 45-60 min by speedboat from Phuket. Tours visit Maya Bay (from the film The Beach), Pileh Lagoon, Viking Cave, snorkel spots and often Bamboo Island. At Maya Bay boats stop at a pier in Loh Samah Bay and you walk in. Swimming is banned there: knee-deep wading only.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.766,7.67695,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Similan Islands</name><description><![CDATA[Day trip · Full day<br>A national park of granite islands about 60 km off the Khao Lak coast, with the clearest water and best snorkelling near Phuket. You climb Sail Rock on Island 8 for the famous view of Donald Duck Bay, snorkel between islands and have lunch on Island 4. Open 15 Oct 2026 to 15 May 2027.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>97.64784,8.66548,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Koh Racha Yai</name><description><![CDATA[Day trip · Full day<br>A hilly island 30-45 min by speedboat south of Phuket, with white sand and very clear water. Day boats land at Patok Bay, where you can snorkel straight from the beach. A short walk leads to quieter Siam Bay. Many tours combine Racha with Coral Island.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.36715,7.60779,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Coral Island (Koh Hey)</name><description><![CDATA[Day trip · Half day<br>A small island only 15 min by speedboat from Chalong or Rawai. Most boats land at busy Long Beach with restaurants, sunbeds and water sports. Banana Beach, further east, is quieter and is mostly visited with its own day packages. Easy snorkelling near the shore. A short and cheap escape.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.37376,7.7459,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Khai Islands (Koh Khai Nok)</name><description><![CDATA[Day trip · Half day<br>Three tiny islands 15-20 min by speedboat from Phuket's east coast. Khai Nok has a white beach with bars and sunbeds. Khai Nai is the largest, with long, shallow sand. Khai Nui has no beach but the best reef: you snorkel from the boat. Short, easy and cheap, but always busy.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.51528,7.89139,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Koh Yao Noi</name><description><![CDATA[Day trip · Full day<br>A quiet, green island in Phang Nga Bay, 30 min by speedboat from Phuket. Rent a scooter, ride past rice fields and small villages, swim at Pasai or Klong Jark beach and kayak to Koh Nok. Views over the limestone islands of the bay. Mostly Muslim and not a party island: a real break.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.60972,8.13333,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Koh Hong (Krabi): lagoon island</name><description><![CDATA[Day trip · Full day<br>A limestone island between Koh Yao Noi and Krabi. Boats go into a shallow lagoon ringed by tall cliffs, and there are two white-sand beaches with clear water. Steep stairs lead to a viewpoint. It is part of a national park and is busy from late morning.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.67806,8.07861,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Railay Beach (Krabi)</name><description><![CDATA[Day trip · Full day<br>A beach area in Krabi with no roads, closed in by huge limestone cliffs, so you arrive by boat. West Railay is a beautiful sunset beach and Phra Nang Cave Beach is close by. Famous for rock climbing. A direct ferry from Phuket makes a long day trip possible, but one or two nights is better.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.83779,8.01154,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Khao Sok: Cheow Lan Lake overnight</name><description><![CDATA[Day trip · 2+ days<br>A huge jungle lake with limestone cliffs in Khao Sok National Park. Longtail boats take you from the dam pier to floating raft houses. You sleep on the water, swim, and kayak in the morning mist. A 1-day tour exists but is very long (about 15 hours), so one night is better.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.82025,8.97782,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Samet Nangshe viewpoint (sunrise)</name><description><![CDATA[Day trip · Half day<br>A hilltop viewpoint over Phang Nga Bay: green mangroves and dozens of limestone islands in the morning mist. Come for sunrise. From the car park you walk up about 20 minutes or take a pickup truck. There are two viewpoints on the way up.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.43864,8.23929,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Koh Phangan rave trip (2-5 days)</name><description><![CDATA[Day trip · 2+ days<br>Thailand's party island, in the Gulf. Most jungle raves are inland near Ban Tai. With the group: OXA (Fri 8 and 15 Jan), Lost Jungle psytrance (Sat 9 to Mon 11) and Halfmoon (Fri 15 - Sat 16). In full-moon week: OXA (Tue 19), Waterfall (Wed 20), Jungle Experience (Thu 21) and the Full Moon Party (Fri 22 Jan).]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>100.03195,9.71735,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>One Chun</name><description><![CDATA[Must-see · 1–2 h<br>Phuket family recipes in an old Old Town shophouse with vintage decor. Order the crab meat yellow curry with rice noodles, moo hong (sweet braised pork belly) and fried prawns in tamarind sauce. Michelin Bib Gourmand 2026.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.39072,7.88578,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Mee Ton Poe (Hokkien noodles)</name><description><![CDATA[Must-see · 1–2 h<br>Phuket's best-known Hokkien noodle shop, cooking since 1946 at the clock tower circle in Phuket Town. The classic is mee Hokkien: thick yellow noodles fried with pork, seafood and greens in a rich gravy, topped with a soft egg. Add pork satay. Simple, fast and cheap.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.39209,7.88001,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Lock Tien (Phuket street dishes)</name><description><![CDATA[Hidden gem · 1–2 h<br>A Phuket Town classic for local Hokkien-Chinese dishes in one place: fried Hokkien noodles, fresh spring rolls (popia sot), o-tao (taro and oyster omelette), lo ba (fried pork and tofu) and o-aew jelly dessert. It has moved from its old corner food court to a shophouse on Bangkok Road.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-gem</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.38644,7.88118,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Go Benz (late-night rice soup)</name><description><![CDATA[Hidden gem · 1–2 h<br>A corner shop open at night, known for kuay jap (rolled rice noodles in peppery pork broth) and khao tom (rice soup), with crispy pork belly on the side. Open until about 1:30 at night, so it is perfect after a party. Michelin Bib Gourmand every year since 2019.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-gem</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.38255,7.88485,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Naam Yoi (Southern Thai curries)</name><description><![CDATA[Hidden gem · 1–2 h<br>A small, simple local place known for rich, very aromatic Southern Thai curries, cooked to order with produce bought at dawn. Try kaeng som (sour fish curry with tamarind) and kaeng pa (jungle curry). No English menu and plastic chairs, but real local flavour. Michelin Bib Gourmand 2026.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-gem</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.40315,7.9008,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Mor Mu Dong (mangrove seafood)</name><description><![CDATA[Hidden gem · 1–2 h<br>Southern Thai food in open wooden huts over a mangrove canal near Chalong, about 10 km from Phuket Town. Mostly local diners. Live seafood waits in tanks by the open kitchen. Try stuffed mackerel, salt-fried pork, sea grape salad, lime squid and salt-crusted fish. Michelin Bib Gourmand.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-gem</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.37198,7.84313,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Malin Plaza night market (Patong)</name><description><![CDATA[Must-see · 1–2 h<br>A big covered night market at the south end of Patong. The front half is food: grills, seafood on ice that they cook for you, pad thai, fruit, pancakes and mango sticky rice, with shared tables. The back half sells clothes and souvenirs. Touristy and warm (no air-con), but cheap for Patong.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.29318,7.88264,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Karon Beach</name><description><![CDATA[Must-see · Half day<br>A wide 3 km beach of soft, pale sand between Patong and Kata. Most hotels are across the beach road, so the sand rarely feels crowded. From December to April the sea is usually calm for swimming. The dry sand squeaks under your feet. Good for long walks at sunset.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.2936,7.8439,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Kamala Beach</name><description><![CDATA[Must-see · Half day<br>About 2 km of soft, pale sand with shade trees. The quiet town behind it grew from a Muslim fishing village. It is the base suggested in this guide. In the high season the sea is shallow, calm and clear, one of the easiest swims on the island. Small Thai restaurants and bamboo bars sit on the sand, good for sunset.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.2831,7.9569,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Surin Beach</name><description><![CDATA[Must-see · Half day<br>An 800 m bay of soft, pale sand with casuarina trees for shade, 5-10 minutes north of Kamala. Between 2023 and May 2025 the bars, sunbeds and beach massage were removed from the sand, so it looks natural again. From December to April the water is often clear and calm: some of the best swimming on the island.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.2785,7.9755,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Plane spotting at Mai Khao Beach</name><description><![CDATA[Must-see · 1–2 h<br>At the south end of Mai Khao Beach, planes pass very low over your head just before they land at Phuket Airport. In the high season the wind comes from the east, so most planes come in over the sea and the sand. It is loud, a little crazy and free. Drink and food stalls wait at the car park and the runway end.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.302,8.1119,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bangla Boxing Stadium (Muay Thai fight night)</name><description><![CDATA[Must-see · Evening<br>Patong's Muay Thai stadium, open since 2004, with fights every night. A card has about 8 bouts, from teenagers up to the main fights, with live traditional music and the Wai Kru dance before each bout. An English commentator explains the action. It is for tourists and not cheap, but a fun first look at Thai boxing.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-place</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3012,7.8915,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Blue Elephant Cooking School (Phuket Old Town)</name><description><![CDATA[Hidden gem · Half day<br>A Thai cooking class in a restored governor's mansion, more than 100 years old, in Phuket Old Town. You cook 4-5 dishes in half a day, then eat them in the restaurant. The morning class starts with a visit to a local market. The afternoon class adds a Thai dessert. The dishes change every day.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-gem</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3848,7.8856,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Renew Sauna &amp; Ice Bath (Bang Tao)</name><description><![CDATA[Hidden gem · 2–3 h<br>A modern sauna and ice-bath club near Boat Avenue in Bang Tao, about 10-15 minutes from Kamala. It has a Finnish sauna, a steam room, a hot pool, ice plunges and a large pool, plus a cafe with healthy food. Hot-cold rounds help you recover the day after a party. Only for guests aged 16 and over.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-gem</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3082,7.9926,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Nai Thon Beach</name><description><![CDATA[Hidden gem · Half day<br>A quiet, sandy bay of about 1 km between two green headlands, 10-15 minutes from the airport. In the dry season the sea is usually clear and good for swimming. A few small restaurants, a minimart and massage shops are across the beach road. Much calmer than the big west-coast beaches.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-gem</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.2776,8.0579,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Natural Restaurant (airport branch)</name><description><![CDATA[Hidden gem · 1–2 h<br>Family-run Southern Thai restaurant since 1992, in a tropical garden with a waterfall. The long picture menu has fresh Andaman seafood such as fish and prawns, curries made with house curry pastes, and spicy salads. Air-conditioned rooms too. A relaxed last meal close to the airport.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-gem</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3145749,8.0933334,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Sabai Massage &amp; Spa (airport branch)</name><description><![CDATA[Hidden gem · 1–2 h<br>Massage and spa shop near the airport with a very high rating (Google 4.9 from 2,050 reviews). Thai, oil, foot, herbal-compress and head-and-shoulder massages in air-conditioned rooms. A good way to spend the last hours before a long flight, and they can drive you to the terminal.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-gem</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3060675,8.0970359,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder>
<Folder><name>Hotels</name><Placemark><name>Luxurious SeaView Pool Villa</name><description><![CDATA[Luxury · 241,500 THB (≈2,610,000 AMD) for 10 nights (8-18 Jan, 8 guests), all Airbnb fees included, after a discount from 283,500 THB (≈3,060,000 AMD). About 24,150 THB (≈261,000 AMD) a night, or 3,020 THB (≈32,600 AMD) per person a night. Checked 17 Oct 2026.<br>Four bedrooms, a marble pool off the living room and a rooftop jacuzzi over Chalong Bay, about 100 m from Friendship Beach. Sleeps 11, so there is room to spare for 8.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-hotel</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.33697,7.80056,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Fantastic SeaView Pool Villa</name><description><![CDATA[Mid-range · 217,700 THB (≈2,350,000 AMD) for 10 nights (8-18 Jan, 8 guests), all Airbnb fees included, after a discount from 255,500 THB (≈2,760,000 AMD). About 21,770 THB (≈235,000 AMD) a night, or 2,720 THB (≈29,400 AMD) per person a night. Checked 17 Oct 2026.<br>The sister villa of the Luxurious SeaView, by the same hosts: four bedrooms, a marble pool off the living room, a lift between floors and a roof terrace over Chalong Bay. The cheaper of the two, for up to 10.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-hotel</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3369,7.80094,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Luxury 4-Bedroom Saltwater Pool Villa</name><description><![CDATA[Luxury · Not available for 8-18 Jan 2027: Airbnb shows the dates as taken. Try nearby dates or message the host. Checked 17 Oct 2026.<br>A new villa in a quiet gated estate 5 minutes from Rawai and Nai Harn beaches, with a saltwater pool and a shallow beach area. A guest favourite in the top 10% on Airbnb, but your dates are already booked.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-hotel</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3267,7.7911,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>SawanSa 3BR Seaview Townhouse #34A</name><description><![CDATA[Luxury · 232,110 THB (≈2,510,000 AMD) for 10 nights (8-18 Jan, 8 guests), all Airbnb fees included, after a discount from 255,400 THB (≈2,760,000 AMD). About 23,210 THB (≈251,000 AMD) a night, or 2,900 THB (≈31,300 AMD) per person a night. Checked 17 Oct 2026.<br>A four-level luxury townhouse on Patong's north hill with panoramic sea views from the roof, a 5-minute walk to the beach and 3 minutes by taxi to Bangla Road. Daily maid service, electricity and drinking water are included.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-hotel</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3022,7.9068,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Modern 4-Bedroom Pool Villa near Laguna</name><description><![CDATA[Mid-range · 206,630 THB (≈2,230,000 AMD) for 10 nights (8-18 Jan, 8 guests), all Airbnb fees included. About 20,660 THB (≈223,000 AMD) a night, or 2,580 THB (≈27,900 AMD) per person a night. Checked 17 Oct 2026.<br>A modern four-bedroom pool villa in an estate between Laguna and Layan Beach, a walk from shops and restaurants. Weekly cleaning is included, and the host can book tours, a cook, massages and transport.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-hotel</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.32437,8.0206,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Spacious 4BR Home near Blue Tree</name><description><![CDATA[Mid-range · 207,000 THB (≈2,240,000 AMD) for 10 nights (8-18 Jan, 8 guests), all Airbnb fees included. About 20,700 THB (≈224,000 AMD) a night, or 2,590 THB (≈28,000 AMD) per person a night. Checked 17 Oct 2026.<br>A big family home (480 m²) a few minutes' drive from Bang Tao Beach, Laguna, Boat Avenue and Blue Tree, with a private pool, four en-suite king bedrooms and two living rooms. Excellent reviews.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-hotel</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3195,7.9962,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>LuxPride 2 by Wallaya Villas (V7)</name><description><![CDATA[Luxury · 261,410 THB (≈2,820,000 AMD) for 10 nights (8-18 Jan, 8 guests), all Airbnb fees included. About 26,140 THB (≈282,000 AMD) a night, or 3,270 THB (≈35,300 AMD) per person a night. Checked 17 Oct 2026.<br>A designer villa with a cedar roof, floor-to-ceiling windows and a garden pool, a few minutes' drive from Laguna and Layan Beach. Strict house rules and extra costs, so read them first.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-hotel</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.32464,8.01865,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>La Belle Pool Villa</name><description><![CDATA[Mid-range · 229,139 THB (≈2,470,000 AMD) for 10 nights (8-18 Jan, 8 guests), all Airbnb fees included. About 22,910 THB (≈247,000 AMD) a night, or 2,860 THB (≈30,900 AMD) per person a night. Checked 17 Oct 2026.<br>A two-storey tropical villa (402 m²) in the green Wallaya Villa Harmony estate, 5 km from Bang Tao Beach, with a large pool, a hot tub and a garden. A quiet base with mountain views and a long record of good reviews.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-hotel</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3212,8.0003,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Alisa Pool Villa</name><description><![CDATA[Luxury · 240,000 THB (≈2,590,000 AMD) for 10 nights (8-18 Jan, 8 guests), all Airbnb fees included. About 24,000 THB (≈259,000 AMD) a night, or 3,000 THB (≈32,400 AMD) per person a night. Checked 17 Oct 2026.<br>A contemporary four-bedroom pool villa in a gated community in Bang Tao: Blue Tree is about 5 minutes away, Boat Avenue and Porto de Phuket about 8.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-hotel</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3228,8.0021,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Brand-New 4BR Villa, Bang Tao</name><description><![CDATA[Budget · 150,000 THB (≈1,620,000 AMD) for 10 nights (8-18 Jan, 8 guests), all Airbnb fees included. About 15,000 THB (≈162,000 AMD) a night, or 1,880 THB (≈20,300 AMD) per person a night. Checked 17 Oct 2026.<br>The cheapest villa on this list: a brand-new four-bedroom house with a private pool in the heart of Bang Tao, 150,000 THB (≈1,620,000 AMD) for all 10 nights. Sleeps 9.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-hotel</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.32136,8.0059,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>3BR Pool Villa by Laguna, Bang Tao</name><description><![CDATA[Budget · 181,741 THB (≈1,960,000 AMD) for 10 nights (8-18 Jan, 8 guests), all Airbnb fees included, after a discount from 201,741 THB (≈2,180,000 AMD). About 18,170 THB (≈196,000 AMD) a night, or 2,270 THB (≈24,500 AMD) per person a night. Checked 17 Oct 2026.<br>A private pool villa with a courtyard, 3 to 5 minutes' drive from Bang Tao Beach, 100 m from the main road and next to Laguna. Only 3 bedrooms for 8, but the host has 16 villas here if you need more rooms.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-hotel</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3078,8.0019,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Laguna Park 5BR Pool Villa</name><description><![CDATA[Luxury · 240,000 THB (≈2,590,000 AMD) for 10 nights (8-18 Jan, 8 guests), all Airbnb fees included, after a discount from 300,000 THB (≈3,240,000 AMD). About 24,000 THB (≈259,000 AMD) a night, or 3,000 THB (≈32,400 AMD) per person a night. Checked 17 Oct 2026.<br>A renovated five-bedroom villa in Laguna Park, among parks and golf courses, a 10-minute walk from Bang Tao Beach with a free shuttle bus. Enough bedrooms for most of the group to have their own.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-hotel</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3023,8.0011,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Lux Laguna Park 5BR, Rooftop Pool</name><description><![CDATA[Luxury · 281,261 THB (≈3,040,000 AMD) for 10 nights (8-18 Jan, 8 guests), all Airbnb fees included. About 28,130 THB (≈304,000 AMD) a night, or 3,520 THB (≈38,000 AMD) per person a night. Checked 17 Oct 2026.<br>A recently renovated five-bedroom villa in Laguna Park with a rooftop pool, near Bang Tao Beach and Boat Avenue. Professionally managed and a guest favourite; the most expensive on this list.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-hotel</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.302,8.0005,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Diamond Villa 278</name><description><![CDATA[Luxury · 250,000 THB (≈2,700,000 AMD) for 10 nights (8-18 Jan, 8 guests), all Airbnb fees included. About 25,000 THB (≈270,000 AMD) a night, or 3,130 THB (≈33,800 AMD) per person a night. Checked 17 Oct 2026.<br>A five-bedroom pool villa in Choeng Thale, between Bang Tao and Surin, for up to 10. The listing has almost no description, so ask the host for details before booking.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-hotel</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.28979,7.979,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Chill Beach Bangla Pool House</name><description><![CDATA[Mid-range · 187,569 THB (≈2,030,000 AMD) for 10 nights (8-18 Jan, 8 adults): 183,569 THB (≈1,980,000 AMD) (9% off 202,300) plus 4,000 THB (≈43,200 AMD) taxes and charges. About 18,760 THB (≈203,000 AMD) a night, or 2,340 THB (≈25,300 AMD) per person a night. Checked 17 Oct 2026.<br>A three-bedroom holiday home with its own pool, 500 m from Bangla Road and under 1 km from Patong Beach. The way to sleep right next to Patong's nightlife.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-hotel</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.30131,7.8934,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Light &amp; Hope Laguna Park 6BR Villa</name><description><![CDATA[Mid-range · 199,136 THB (≈2,150,000 AMD) for 10 nights (8-18 Jan, 8 guests), all Airbnb fees included, with the host's weekly discount. About 19,910 THB (≈215,000 AMD) a night, or 2,490 THB (≈26,900 AMD) per person a night. Checked 17 Oct 2026.<br>Six bedrooms on three floors in Laguna Park 2, a gated villa estate in Laguna Phuket, with a free estate shuttle to Bang Tao Beach. It sleeps 14: the most bedrooms on this list.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-hotel</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.31218,8.02253,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Mouana Breeze Mai Khao 4BR Pool Villa</name><description><![CDATA[Luxury · 233,568 THB (≈2,520,000 AMD) for 10 nights (8-18 Jan, 8 guests), all Airbnb fees included, after a weekly discount from 259,520 THB (≈2,800,000 AMD). About 23,360 THB (≈252,000 AMD) a night, or 2,920 THB (≈31,500 AMD) per person a night. Electricity is extra. Checked 17 Oct 2026.<br>A new villa (built 2024) in the north, 900 m from Mai Khao Beach and 15 minutes from the airport. Four bedrooms, each with its own bathroom and a king bed, around an 8 x 4 m saltwater pool.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-hotel</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.31116,8.12952,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Patong Villa 5BR with Pool and Game Room</name><description><![CDATA[Mid-range · 202,181 THB (≈2,180,000 AMD) for 10 nights (8-18 Jan, 8 guests), all Airbnb fees included. About 20,220 THB (≈218,000 AMD) a night, or 2,530 THB (≈27,300 AMD) per person a night. Electricity and water are included. Checked 17 Oct 2026.<br>Five bedrooms and six bathrooms on a quiet street in Patong, with a pool, a jacuzzi and a games room with a pool table. You can walk to the shops and markets, and Bangla Road is about 1 km away.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-hotel</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3,7.8831,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bang Tao 4BR Villa, Unit 1</name><description><![CDATA[Mid-range · 210,072 THB (≈2,270,000 AMD) for 10 nights (8-18 Jan, 8 guests), all Airbnb fees included. About 21,010 THB (≈227,000 AMD) a night, or 2,630 THB (≈28,400 AMD) per person a night. Checked 17 Oct 2026.<br>Four bedrooms, each with its own bathroom and hot tub, floor-to-ceiling windows and a door straight onto the pool in the courtyard. Renovated in April 2025, in the villa area between Bang Tao Beach and Laguna.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-hotel</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3091,8.0041,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Tropical 4BR Pool Villa, Rawai</name><description><![CDATA[Budget · 180,000 THB (≈1,940,000 AMD) for 10 nights (8-18 Jan, 8 guests), all Airbnb fees included. About 18,000 THB (≈194,000 AMD) a night, or 2,250 THB (≈24,300 AMD) per person a night. Electricity is extra. Checked 17 Oct 2026.<br>A new two-storey villa with a private pool in a quiet, green street in Rawai, near shops and cafés. Four bedrooms with king beds for the 8 of you, at one of the lower prices on this list.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-hotel</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3081,7.7878,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Brand-New 4BR Villa with Gym, Rawai</name><description><![CDATA[Budget · 180,000 THB (≈1,940,000 AMD) for 10 nights (8-18 Jan, 8 guests), all Airbnb fees included. About 18,000 THB (≈194,000 AMD) a night, or 2,250 THB (≈24,300 AMD) per person a night. Electricity is extra. Checked 17 Oct 2026.<br>A new villa with its own pool in a quiet, gated street in Rawai, a short drive from Nai Harn Beach. Four bedrooms with king beds, plus a shared gym and pool table for the guests of the estate.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-hotel</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3221,7.7809,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Sunshine Pool Villa, Bangla Patong</name><description><![CDATA[Luxury · 241,400 THB (≈2,610,000 AMD) for 10 nights (8-18 Jan, 8 guests), all Airbnb fees included. About 24,140 THB (≈261,000 AMD) a night, or 3,020 THB (≈32,600 AMD) per person a night. Checked 17 Oct 2026.<br>A private pool villa in the middle of Patong: about 5 minutes on foot to Bangla Road, Patong Beach and the Jungceylon mall, so nobody needs a taxi at night. An Airbnb guest favourite (4.91, 46 reviews).]]></description><styleUrl>#p-hotel</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3011,7.8941,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Villa Take-it-Easy, Kamala</name><description><![CDATA[Budget · 141,000 THB (≈1,520,000 AMD) for 10 nights (8-18 Jan, 8 guests), all Airbnb fees included. About 14,100 THB (≈152,000 AMD) a night, or 1,760 THB (≈19,000 AMD) per person a night. Checked 17 Oct 2026.<br>The lowest price on this list, in a private estate in Kamala (the base this guide recommends), a walk from the beach, restaurants and shops. Only 2 bathrooms for 8 people.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-hotel</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.2904,7.9529,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>88 Pool Villa Patong, 6BR</name><description><![CDATA[Luxury · 274,750 THB (≈2,970,000 AMD) for 10 nights (8-18 Jan, 8 guests), all Airbnb fees included. About 27,480 THB (≈297,000 AMD) a night, or 3,430 THB (≈37,000 AMD) per person a night. Checked 17 Oct 2026.<br>Six bedrooms on two floors in a quiet village in central Patong, 13 minutes on foot to Patong Beach and 750 m from Jungceylon: room for everyone, with the nightlife in walking distance.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-hotel</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.2976,7.884,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Oak Tree Villa Patong</name><description><![CDATA[Mid-range · 236,230 THB (≈2,550,000 AMD) for 10 nights (8-18 Jan, 8 guests), all Airbnb fees included. About 23,620 THB (≈255,000 AMD) a night, or 2,950 THB (≈31,900 AMD) per person a night. Checked 17 Oct 2026.<br>A private pool villa a short walk from Patong Beach and Bangla Road, with four king bedrooms, five bathrooms and a rooftop BBQ terrace. Earlier guests rated it only 3.91 (11 reviews): read the reviews before booking.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-hotel</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.29874,7.88356,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Stunning 4BR Pool Villa with Pool Table, Bangla Patong</name><description><![CDATA[Luxury · 255,000 THB (≈2,750,000 AMD) for 10 nights (8-18 Jan, 8 guests), all Airbnb fees included. About 25,500 THB (≈275,000 AMD) a night, or 3,190 THB (≈34,500 AMD) per person a night. Checked 18 Oct 2026.<br>A private pool villa in the middle of Patong, with a pool table by the pool, a short walk from Bangla Road and the beach. It is a new listing with one review, but the host company (MP Property) has 1,086 reviews averaging 4.77 over 11 years.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-hotel</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.301,7.8935,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>128 Villa: Stylish 4BR Villa with Jacuzzi, Patong</name><description><![CDATA[Budget · 182,100 THB (≈1,970,000 AMD) for 10 nights (8-18 Jan, 8 guests), all Airbnb fees included, after a weekly discount from 202,000 THB (≈2,180,000 AMD). About 18,210 THB (≈197,000 AMD) a night, or 2,280 THB (≈24,600 AMD) per person a night. Checked 18 Oct 2026.<br>One of the cheaper villas for the group: a private pool and a jacuzzi in a quiet lane in central Patong, about 13 minutes on foot from the beach, rated 4.83 by 46 guests. Only 5 beds (three kings and two singles), so most of you share a bed.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-hotel</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.2965,7.8845,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Elite Atoll Luxury Pool Villa D, Rawai</name><description><![CDATA[Mid-range · 194,219 THB (≈2,100,000 AMD) for 10 nights (8-18 Jan, 8 guests), all Airbnb fees included, after a weekly discount from 215,410 THB (≈2,330,000 AMD). About 19,420 THB (≈210,000 AMD) a night, or 2,430 THB (≈26,200 AMD) per person a night. Electricity and water are extra. Checked 18 Oct 2026.<br>A two-storey pool villa in the quiet Sai Yuan area of Rawai, with an en-suite bathroom for every bedroom, an open-plan kitchen and a BBQ by the pool. Careful: its only review so far gives it 1 out of 5, though the host company (a Superhost) averages 4.53 from 38 reviews. Only 4 beds for 8 of you.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-hotel</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3249,7.7945,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>The SOL Residences (4BR), Sai Yuan, Rawai</name><description><![CDATA[Luxury · 251,200 THB (≈2,710,000 AMD) for 10 nights (8-18 Jan, 8 guests), all Airbnb fees included, after a discount from 314,000 THB (≈3,390,000 AMD). About 25,120 THB (≈271,000 AMD) a night, or 3,140 THB (≈33,900 AMD) per person a night. Checked 18 Oct 2026.<br>A new luxury house in the quiet Sai Yuan area of Rawai, about 370 m² with a saltwater pool, a jacuzzi and a sundeck for sunsets, run by a big Superhost company (1,087 reviews, 4.84) with 24-hour guest help. Careful: quiet hours from 20:00 to 07:00, so no parties at the house.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-hotel</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.3168,7.7964,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder>
<Folder><name>Money changers</name><Placemark><name>Mamy Exchange · Mamy Exchange Phuket (Koh Kaew)</name><description><![CDATA[Mon-Fri 08:00-17:00, Sat-Sun 09:00-16:30 (Google listing; call to confirm)<br>The best rate we could check in Phuket. On 15 Oct 2026 Mamy paid 33.35 THB for USD 50-100 notes and 37.35 THB for a euro, about 0.5% under the mid-market rate. It has one shop, in Koh Kaew on route 402 (airport to Phuket Town). Live rates are on its website.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-money</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.377564,7.964143,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Lion Currency Exchange · Lion Currency Exchange Patong (Jungceylon)</name><description><![CDATA[Daily 09:00-21:00 (Google listing)<br>The best choice in Patong by reviews. Lion has a booth on the Jungceylon ground floor (shop GC4118, by the Big C entrance), open daily 09:00-21:00, 2 more booths in Jungceylon and a flagship on the 4th floor of Central Phuket Festival. It does not publish rates, so check the board.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-money</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.299421,7.890028,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Lion Currency Exchange · Lion Currency Exchange (Central Phuket Festival flagship)</name><description><![CDATA[<br>The best choice in Patong by reviews. Lion has a booth on the Jungceylon ground floor (shop GC4118, by the Big C entrance), open daily 09:00-21:00, 2 more booths in Jungceylon and a flagship on the 4th floor of Central Phuket Festival. It does not publish rates, so check the board.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-money</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.367244,7.891691,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>SuperRich 1965 Partner (Phuket Old Town) · SuperRich Exchange @ Phuket, Suriyadej Circle (Partner)</name><description><![CDATA[Mon-Sat 10:00-20:00, closed Sunday<br>The only official SuperRich in Phuket. It is a SuperRich 1965 (orange brand) partner shop at the fountain roundabout (Suriyadej Circle) in Old Town, open Mon-Sat 10:00-20:00 and closed on Sunday. Its Phuket rates are not online. The Pattaya partner paid 0.15 THB less than SuperRich Bangkok on 15 Oct 2026.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-money</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.38702,7.88305,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>NC Plus (Thailand) · NC PLUS (Thailand) Co., Ltd.</name><description><![CDATA[Mon-Sat about 09:00-17:00 (OSM says 08:30-18:00), closed Sunday<br>A small exchange office in Phuket Town on Thilok Uthit 2 Rd, in business since 2005. Expat forums have recommended it, and its Google rating is about 4.8. It is open Mon-Sat in office hours and closed on Sunday. It has no online rates, so call 076-355-393 before you go.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-money</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.395469,7.87892,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Value Plus Currency Exchange · Value Plus Currency Exchange (Patong)</name><description><![CDATA[10:00-19:00<br>A chain with booths in Patong, Laguna/Boat Avenue, Porto de Phuket, Central Festival, Floresta and Chalong. Its Phuket rates are not online, so we could not compare them. It is useful late at night: the Soi Sansabai booth in Patong is open until 04:00.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-money</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.301816,7.893812,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Value Plus Currency Exchange · Value Plus Currency Exchange (Soi Sansabai, Patong)</name><description><![CDATA[09:00-04:00<br>A chain with booths in Patong, Laguna/Boat Avenue, Porto de Phuket, Central Festival, Floresta and Chalong. Its Phuket rates are not online, so we could not compare them. It is useful late at night: the Soi Sansabai booth in Patong is open until 04:00.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-money</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.299473,7.89279,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Value Plus Currency Exchange · Value Plus Currency Exchange (Laguna / Boat Avenue)</name><description><![CDATA[09:00-20:00<br>A chain with booths in Patong, Laguna/Boat Avenue, Porto de Phuket, Central Festival, Floresta and Chalong. Its Phuket rates are not online, so we could not compare them. It is useful late at night: the Soi Sansabai booth in Patong is open until 04:00.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-money</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.305652,7.994777,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Value Plus Currency Exchange · Value Plus Currency Exchange (Porto de Phuket)</name><description><![CDATA[09:00-21:30<br>A chain with booths in Patong, Laguna/Boat Avenue, Porto de Phuket, Central Festival, Floresta and Chalong. Its Phuket rates are not online, so we could not compare them. It is useful late at night: the Soi Sansabai booth in Patong is open until 04:00.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-money</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.30531,7.991827,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Value Plus Currency Exchange · Value Plus Currency Exchange (Central Phuket Festival)</name><description><![CDATA[10:30-20:30<br>A chain with booths in Patong, Laguna/Boat Avenue, Porto de Phuket, Central Festival, Floresta and Chalong. Its Phuket rates are not online, so we could not compare them. It is useful late at night: the Soi Sansabai booth in Patong is open until 04:00.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-money</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.36793,7.891519,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Value Plus Currency Exchange · Value Plus Currency Exchange (HomePro Chalong)</name><description><![CDATA[<br>A chain with booths in Patong, Laguna/Boat Avenue, Porto de Phuket, Central Festival, Floresta and Chalong. Its Phuket rates are not online, so we could not compare them. It is useful late at night: the Soi Sansabai booth in Patong is open until 04:00.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-money</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.338988,7.824758,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Money Shop Exchange · Money Shop Exchange Kata</name><description><![CDATA[Mon-Sat 10:00-19:00, closed Sunday<br>A small chain with offices in Kata, Karon, Rawai, Nai Harn, Chalong, Bang Tao, Nai Yang and Central Festival. Its Central Festival office posted USD 33.28 and EUR 37.30 on 14 Oct 2026: OK, but lower than Mamy. Several offices close on Sunday.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-money</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.300501,7.81947,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Money Shop Exchange · Money Shop Exchange Karon</name><description><![CDATA[Mon-Sun 10:00-19:00 (website)<br>A small chain with offices in Kata, Karon, Rawai, Nai Harn, Chalong, Bang Tao, Nai Yang and Central Festival. Its Central Festival office posted USD 33.28 and EUR 37.30 on 14 Oct 2026: OK, but lower than Mamy. Several offices close on Sunday.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-money</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.295213,7.829886,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Money Shop Exchange · Money Shop Rawai</name><description><![CDATA[Mon-Sun 10:00-19:00 (website). Google lists Mon-Fri 10:00-18:00, Sat 10:00-17:00, closed Sunday<br>A small chain with offices in Kata, Karon, Rawai, Nai Harn, Chalong, Bang Tao, Nai Yang and Central Festival. Its Central Festival office posted USD 33.28 and EUR 37.30 on 14 Oct 2026: OK, but lower than Mamy. Several offices close on Sunday.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-money</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.31935,7.770813,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Money Shop Exchange · Money Shop Exchange Nai Harn</name><description><![CDATA[Mon-Sat 10:00-19:00, closed Sunday<br>A small chain with offices in Kata, Karon, Rawai, Nai Harn, Chalong, Bang Tao, Nai Yang and Central Festival. Its Central Festival office posted USD 33.28 and EUR 37.30 on 14 Oct 2026: OK, but lower than Mamy. Several offices close on Sunday.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-money</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.317447,7.783255,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Money Shop Exchange · Money Shop Chalong (Lotus&#39;s)</name><description><![CDATA[Mon-Sat 10:00-19:00, closed Sunday<br>A small chain with offices in Kata, Karon, Rawai, Nai Harn, Chalong, Bang Tao, Nai Yang and Central Festival. Its Central Festival office posted USD 33.28 and EUR 37.30 on 14 Oct 2026: OK, but lower than Mamy. Several offices close on Sunday.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-money</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.33387,7.839961,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Money Shop Exchange · Money Shop Exchange Nai Yang</name><description><![CDATA[Mon-Sat 10:00-19:00, closed Sunday (website)<br>A small chain with offices in Kata, Karon, Rawai, Nai Harn, Chalong, Bang Tao, Nai Yang and Central Festival. Its Central Festival office posted USD 33.28 and EUR 37.30 on 14 Oct 2026: OK, but lower than Mamy. Several offices close on Sunday.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-money</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.30066,8.086658,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Money Shop Exchange · Money Shop Exchange (Central Phuket Festival)</name><description><![CDATA[Mon-Sun 10:00-22:00 (website)<br>A small chain with offices in Kata, Karon, Rawai, Nai Harn, Chalong, Bang Tao, Nai Yang and Central Festival. Its Central Festival office posted USD 33.28 and EUR 37.30 on 14 Oct 2026: OK, but lower than Mamy. Several offices close on Sunday.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-money</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.367244,7.891691,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Phuket Airport exchange counters (HKT) · Phuket International Airport, international terminal arrivals</name><description><![CDATA[<br>Exchange counters and bank ATMs are in the arrivals hall. Use the counters only for a small amount, for the taxi and your first meal. Local guides from 2026 say airport rates are 3-5% below town rates. Bank ATMs charge 250-350 THB (≈2,700-3,800 AMD) for each withdrawal.]]></description><styleUrl>#p-money</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>98.305702,8.105882,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder>
</Document></kml>
